  "question": {
    "text": "The probability of a man hitting a target is $\\frac{2}{5}$. He fires at the target $k$ times $(k$, a given number). Then the minimum $k$, so that the probability of hitting the target at least once is more than $\\frac{7}{10}$, is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n3\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n5\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n4",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{3}{5} \\times \\frac{2}{5}+\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2 \\times \\frac{2}{5}+\\ldots \\ldots+\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^k \\cdot \\frac{2}{5}>\\frac{7}{10} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{2}{5}\\left[1+\\frac{3}{5}+\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2+\\ldots \\ldots+\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^k\\right]>\\frac{7}{10} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{2}{5} \\times \\frac{1-\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^k}{1-\\frac{3}{5}}>\\frac{7}{10} \\Rightarrow 1-\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^k>\\frac{7}{10} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^k < \\frac{3}{10} \\Rightarrow k \\geq 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHence minimum value of $k=3$"
  }
}